From: PanVK Kbase Android contributors
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost/clc: defer global initializers until specialization

Purpose: Preserve shared constant-array initialization in every libpan kernel
variant. Lowering shader-global initializers on the multi-entrypoint library
consumes them into its first entrypoint, leaving other kernels uninitialized.
Source/Reference: Local per-pass SPIR-V/NIR audit of the pinned Mesa 27 tree;
nir_lower_variable_initializers consumes constant_initializer after emitting
stores in an entrypoint.
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (moto g86 5G, Android 16).
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 13baeb70c066a9f82d2bcfb29f06e4865212affa (27.0.0-devel).
Dependencies: None.
Validation test: Recompile libpan triangle tess_gen and fused count_draw from
unchanged SPIR-V; verify all 80 shared source bytes are initialized in each
specialized entrypoint. Large_Draw direct/indirect passed 8/8 at 64, 507, 508
and 70000 patches without debug sync. Full Large_Draw, fan opt-in (41 cases),
tessellation, conditional tessellation and XFB standalone tests passed.

Keep lowering function-local initializers after constant localization, but
retain shared global initializers until linking leaves a single entrypoint.
This fixes the initializer lifetime rather than adding tessellator field
stores or changing TLS sizes.

--- a/src/panfrost/clc/pan_compile.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/clc/pan_compile.c
@@ -133,9 +133,9 @@
    nir_lower_constant_to_temp(nir);
-
+
-   /* We can go ahead and lower the rest of the constant initializers.  We do
+   /* We can go ahead and lower the function-local constant initializers.  We do
     * this here so that nir_remove_dead_variables and split_per_member_structs
     * below see the corresponding stores.
     */
-   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_variable_initializers, ~0);
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_variable_initializers, nir_var_function_temp);
-
+
    /* LLVM loves take advantage of the fact that vec3s in OpenCL are 16B
@@ -378,4 +378,5 @@
          nir_link_shader_functions(s, nir);
          NIR_PASS(_, s, nir_inline_functions);
          nir_remove_non_entrypoints(s);
+         NIR_PASS(_, s, nir_lower_variable_initializers, ~0);
          NIR_PASS(_, s, nir_opt_deref);
